# The whole-project checks, run once per push rather than once per commit.
#
# `lint` and `format` are omitted: pre-commit already ran both over every staged file,
# so repeating them across the entire tree here would only catch damage done outside
# git — which CI covers. What pre-commit structurally cannot catch is the class of
# breakage that spans files: a type error introduced in an untouched consumer, an
# architectural boundary crossed transitively, a test broken elsewhere. That is exactly
# this list.
npm run typecheck && npm run arch:check && npm test -- --silent
